l_call","event_action":"tool_execution","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7","event_data":{"event_id": "db161780-6a85-441c-ab76-9844b3cff84a", "tool_name": "events_list", "event_type": "aiagent.llm.tool_call", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7", "tool_result": "### Incident summary\n\n- **Workload:** Deployment `demo-ingress/api-gateway`\n- **Node:** `kubernaut-remote-cluster-control-plane`\n- **Image:** `quay.io/kubernaut-cicd/demo-http-server:1.0.0`\n- **Observed period:** 2026-10-02 04:18–04:35 UTC\n\n### Timeline and impact\n\n1. At approximately **04:18 UTC**, Deployment `api-gateway` initiated a rollout:\n   - ReplicaSet `api-gateway-6b89c75755` scaled from **0 to 5**.\n   - Five pods were scheduled and started successfully.\n2. During startup, health checks began failing:\n   - `/healthz` on port **8080** returned **connection refused**.\n   - One readiness check also timed out while awaiting response headers.\n3. At **04:18:41**, pod `api-gateway-67b95bfdbf-ptzc9` was stopped and deleted. Its readiness probe had failed with both connection-refused and timeout errors.\n4. The Deployment progressively replaced the old ReplicaSet:\n   - `api-gateway-6b89c75755` reduced from **5 to 4**.\n   - New ReplicaSet `api-gateway-67b95bfdbf` increased from **0 to 3** by 04:18:41.\n5. The replacement pods (`k7qxs`, `ntqnh`, and `qvlfx`) repeatedly failed readiness and liveness probes against port 8080:\n   - Liveness failures caused container restarts.\n   - By approximately **04:34–04:35**, Kubernetes reported **BackOff restarting failed container `api-gateway`**.\n   - Containers were recreated and restarted around **04:25–04:35**, but probe failures continued.\n\n### Key findings\n\n- The container image was already present on the node and was pulled successfully; there is no evidence of an image-pull failure.\n- Scheduling and container startup succeeded.\n- The primary failure is that the application was not accepting connections or responding reliably on **port 8080**, causing readiness/liveness failures, restarts, and CrashLoopBackOff-style backoff behavior.\n- Events show inconsistent ordering between probe timestamps and container lifecycle events, so pod-level status and container logs should be consulted to establish the exact restart sequence.", "tool_arguments": {"namespace": "demo-ingress"}, "tool_call_index": 3, "tool_result_preview": "### Incident summary\n\n- **Workload:** Deployment `demo-ingress/api-gateway`\n- **Node:** `kubernaut-remote-cluster-control-plane`\n- **Image:** `quay.io/kubernaut-cicd/demo-http-server:1.0.0`\n- **Observed period:** 2026-10-02 04:18–04:35 UTC\n\n### Timeline and impact\n\n1. At approximately **04:18 UTC**, Deployment `api-gateway` initiated a rollout:\n   - ReplicaSet `api-gateway-6b89c75755` scaled from **0 to 5**.\n   - Five pods were scheduled and started successfully.\n2. During startup, health chec"}}, {"event_id":"59309d89-4207-480c-b0b9-d2ef75c68aab","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:36:36+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.llm.response","event_action":"llm_response","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7","event_data":{"event_id": "6650c6c4-d4fb-437f-9831-0f9ae3fc4a39", "event_type": "aiagent.llm.response", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7", "tokens_used": 12744, "has_analysis": false, "analysis_length": 0, "tool_call_count": 9, "analysis_preview": ""}}, {"event_id":"54bf290c-33e1-4636-a610-a82b1d1c1da1","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:36:55+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.llm.tool_call","event_action":"tool_execution","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7","event_data":{"event_id": "4063f5e8-a11d-44a9-b57c-5affee2102f6", "tool_name": "nodes_stats_summary", "event_type": "aiagent.llm.tool_call", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7", "tool_result": "## Incident-focused summary\n\n**Source:** pre-truncated `nodes_stats_summary` output (originally 123,285 characters; 100,000 retained).  \n**Node:** `kubernaut-remote-cluster-control-plane`  \n**Collection time:** approximately `2026-10-02 04:36 UTC`.\n\n### Overall node condition\n\n- **CPU pressure is the dominant issue.**\n  - Node CPU: ~**982 millicores** currently used.\n  - CPU PSI averages: **12.07% full / 22.27% some over 10m**, increasing to **36.86% / 54.93% over 5m**.\n  - The `pods` cgroup is particularly pressured: **39.92% full / 51.83% some over 5m**.\n- **Memory is not currently exhausted.**\n  - ~**11.94 GiB available**; usage ~**3.33 GiB**, working set ~**2.64 GiB**.\n  - Memory PSI is low: ~**0.07% full / 3.12% some over 5m**.\n  - No swap configured or used.\n- **Disk capacity is critically low at the node filesystem level.**\n  - Filesystem capacity: ~**99.25 GB**.\n  - Used: ~**96.25 GB** (**~97% full**).\n  - Available: only ~**3.01 GB**.\n  - Inodes are not constrained: ~**5.93M free of 8.19M**.\n- **Network has no reported errors.**\n  - `eth0`: ~**763.5 MB RX**, **225.7 MB TX**; zero RX/TX errors.\n- **Runtime/image filesystem reports only ~2.57 GB used**, suggesting most node disk consumption is outside container image/container writable layers, likely host-level data, logs, or other filesystem content. This discrepancy should be investigated.\n- **Process limits are not near exhaustion:** `curproc=2,736`, `maxpid=111,179`.\n\n### Highest-impact workloads\n\n#### `kube-apiserver`\n- CPU: ~**311 millicores**; CPU PSI **6.08% full / 8.39% some over 10m**, **34.45% / 39.89% over 5m**.\n- Memory: ~**1.03 GiB**, working set ~**941 MiB**, RSS ~**908 MiB**.\n- Significant cumulative major faults: **43,343**.\n- I/O PSI modest but persistent: **0.46% full / 0.57% some over 10m**.\n- This is a major contributor to control-plane CPU load and should be correlated with API request volume, webhook activity, controller reconciliation, and etcd latency.\n\n#### `prometheus-fleet-spoke-0`\n- Aggregate CPU: ~**128 millicores**; CPU PSI **7.48% full / 8.09% some over 10m**, **37.97% / 39.25% over 5m**.\n- Memory: ~**653 MiB**, working set ~**550 MiB**.\n- Persistent volume usage: ~**466 MB**.\n- Network: ~**2.30 GB RX**, **85 MB TX**.\n- Prometheus is a significant CPU, memory, network, and storage consumer; scrape/query load should be checked.\n\n#### `etcd`\n- CPU: ~**46–47 millicores**, but very high CPU PSI: roughly **5% full / 5.4% some over 10m**, rising to **27–30% over 5m**.\n- Memory: ~**88–92 MiB**, working set ~**75 MiB**.\n- Major page faults: ~**146,000**.\n- I/O PSI: up to ~**0.8–1.0% full**, **~0.9–1.1% some over 10m**.\n- The sustained CPU and I/O pressure are concerning for control-plane responsiveness. Check etcd disk latency, fsync duration, database size/defrag status, and API-server request load.\n\n#### Control-plane controllers\n- `kube-controller-manager`: ~**55–61 millicores**, CPU PSI up to **23–26% over 5m**; memory ~**150–156 MiB**.\n- `kube-scheduler`: ~**26–29 millicores**, CPU PSI up to **19–20% over 5m**.\n- `kube-proxy`: ~**10–11 millicores**, CPU PSI up to **16–18% over 5m**.\n- These indicate broad control-plane CPU contention rather than a single isolated application process.\n\n#### Other elevated system components\n- `cert-manager-cainjector`: ~**7.6 millicores**, CPU PSI ~**20% over 5m**.\n- `cert-manager-controller`: ~**14–16 millicores**, CPU PSI ~**25–27% over 5m**.\n- `istiod`: ~**17–19 millicores**, CPU PSI ~**8–10% over 5m**.\n- `coredns`: CPU PSI approximately **9–10% over 5m**.\n- `metrics-server`: CPU PSI approximately **14–16% over 5m**.\n- These may be victims of node-wide CPU contention, although cert-manager activity may also be contributing to control-plane/API pressure.\n\n### Application workloads\n\n- `api-gateway` replicas:\n  - Low absolute CPU and memory use, generally **~1–3 millicores** and **~8–11 MiB** each.\n  - No meaningful memory or I/O pressure.\n- `checkout-api` replicas:\n  - Low resource usage, approximately **~1–3 millicores** and **~9–10 MiB** each.\n  - No notable memory or I/O pressure.\n- `worker`:\n  - Negligible CPU (~0.45 millicores) and memory (~6.5 MiB).\n- Application pods shown do not appear to be the primary source of the incident.\n\n### Storage observations\n\n- Node filesystem:\n  - **96.25 GB used / 99.25 GB capacity**, only **3.01 GB free**.\n- Individual pod ephemeral-storage usage is generally small.\n- Prometheus persistent data accounts for approximately **466 MB** in the shown metrics.\n- The runtime-reported image/container filesystem is only ~**2.57 GB used**, so the remaining disk consumption likely resides in:\n  - host logs,\n  - Kubernetes/container runtime metadata,\n  - deleted-but-open files,\n  - local-path volumes,\n  - other host directories not represented in the runtime filesystem metrics.\n- Disk pressure may lead to eviction or degraded etcd/API-server performance even though memory remains healthy.\n\n### Timeline clues\n\n- Node and core control-plane components started around **2026-10-01 19:30 UTC**.\n- API gateway replicas restarted around **04:18 UTC**.\n- `metrics-server` restarted around **04:19 UTC**.\n- `cert-manager-webhook` restarted around **04:35 UTC**, only minutes before collection; its short lifetime explains low cumulative CPU totals but it shows elevated recent CPU PSI.\n- `cert-manager-controller` started around **00:01 UTC**.\n- These restarts should be correlated with events, probe failures, node pressure, or deployment activity.\n\n### Most likely incident signals\n\n1. **Node-wide CPU contention**, strongest in the `pods` cgroup and control-plane components.\n2. **Severe node filesystem utilization (~97%)**, with an unexplained gap between node usage and runtime/image/container filesystem usage.\n3. **Control-plane stress**, especially involving `kube-apiserver`, etcd, controller-manager, scheduler, Prometheus, and cert-manager.\n4. **No evidence of memory exhaustion, swap activity, network errors, inode exhaustion, or application-container resource runaway** in the supplied portion.\n\n### Recommended investigation priorities\n\n1. Identify the source of the ~93+ GB not accounted for by runtime/image/container usage:\n   - inspect `/var/log`, container logs, journald, `/var/lib/containerd`, `/var/lib/kubelet`, local-path volumes, and deleted-open files;\n   - check node DiskPressure events and kubelet eviction messages.\n2. Inspect CPU saturation and throttling:\n   - node allocatable CPU, pod requests/limits, cgroup throttling, host steal/iowait;\n   - correlate with API-server, Prometheus, cert-manager, and controller activity.\n3. Check etcd health:\n   - fsync/backend commit latency, WAL growth, database size, compaction/defragmentation, leader changes.\n4. Check API-server load:\n   - request rate/latency, inflight requests, audit logging, watch/list storms, webhook latency and failures.\n5. Correlate the **04:18–04:35 UTC pod restarts** with events, probes, rollout activity, and node pressure.", "tool_arguments": {"name": "kubernaut-remote-cluster-control-plane"}, "tool_call_index": 6, "tool_result_preview": "## Incident-focused summary\n\n**Source:** pre-truncated `nodes_stats_summary` output (originally 123,285 characters; 100,000 retained).  \n**Node:** `kubernaut-remote-cluster-control-plane`  \n**Collection time:** approximately `2026-10-02 04:36 UTC`.\n\n### Overall node condition\n\n- **CPU pressure is the dominant issue.**\n  - Node CPU: ~**982 millicores** currently used.\n  - CPU PSI averages: **12.07% full / 22.27% some over 10m**, increasing to **36.86% / 54.93% over 5m**.\n  - The `pods` cgroup is "}}, {"event_id":"e39fe2f0-c3db-4c83-9f2e-2888017c5863","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:36:55+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.llm.tool_call","event_action":"tool_execution","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7","event_data":{"event_id": "efb0f80f-f896-4bcd-a12b-00cb4e366819", "tool_name": "pods_log", "event_type": "aiagent.llm.tool_call", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7", "tool_res