"tokens_used": 19111, "has_analysis": false, "analysis_length": 0, "tool_call_count": 1, "analysis_preview": ""}}, {"event_id":"99afe300-5863-4633-80f8-ea3205b0ff49","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:37:40+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.rca.complete","event_action":"llm_response","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7","event_data":{"event_id": "d89c5b2e-a96e-4136-8f87-2b796a50a890", "event_type": "aiagent.rca.complete", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7", "response_data": {"analysis": "The three crashing `api-gateway` pods use `gateway-config-bad`, whose `config.yaml` contains unsupported `invalid_directive: true`; the application exits with code 1 during startup, causing probe failures and CrashLoopBackOff.", "warnings": [], "timestamp": "2026-10-02T04:37:40Z", "confidence": 0.97, "incidentId": "rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7", "isActionable": true, "needsHumanReview": false, "rootCauseAnalysis": {"summary": "The three crashing `api-gateway` pods use `gateway-config-bad`, whose `config.yaml` contains unsupported `invalid_directive: true`; the application exits with code 1 during startup, causing probe failures and CrashLoopBackOff.", "severity": "critical", "causalChain": ["Signal: Pods `api-gateway-67b95bfdbf-k7qxs`, `ntqnh`, and `qvlfx` entered CrashLoopBackOff with exit code 1.", "Why? The container terminates during startup, so readiness/liveness probes to `:8080/healthz` receive connection refused and liveness restarts the container.", "Why? The application logs report `invalid directive found in /etc/demo-http-server/config.yaml — aborting`.", "Why? The failing ReplicaSet mounts ConfigMap `gateway-config-bad`, whose `config.yaml` contains `invalid_directive: true`; the healthy ReplicaSet mounts `gateway-config` without that directive.", "Root cause: Invalid application configuration in `demo-ingress/ConfigMap/gateway-config-bad`; replace/remove the invalid directive or update the Deployment to the validated `gateway-config`."], "dueDiligence": {"targetAccuracy": "The target is `ConfigMap/gateway-config-bad`, whose data directly causes the startup failure and can be corrected without targeting the symptom-reporter Deployment. Resource context identifies the same ConfigMap as root owner.", "proportionality": "A single shared ConfigMap is the most specific remediable resource: correcting it fixes all three failing replicas and permits the Deployment rollout to recover. Node pressure is listed as a contributor rather than the primary target because it does not match the direct, evidenced failure mechanism.", "scopeCompleteness": "Inspected the Deployment, both ReplicaSets, all three failing pods, a healthy representative pod, both referenced ConfigMaps, namespace events, node usage/statistics, Service, and Ingress listing. Prometheus and Alertmanager were attempted but inaccessible due to timeouts. Downstream external clients were not inspected because the application fails before serving traffic.", "causalCompleteness": "The chain was traced from CrashLoopBackOff through exit code 1, probe refusal, application startup logs, the mounted file, and the exact invalid ConfigMap key. A deeper cause for why the bad ConfigMap was created is not observable from Kubernetes runtime data.", "evidenceSufficiency": "Supported by Deployment/ReplicaSet manifests, pod status, current and previous logs, ConfigMap contents, events, Service data, node statistics, and pod metrics. Assumption: the intended remediation is to remove `invalid_directive` or switch to `gateway-config`; the original change author/source is unverified. Alertmanager and Prometheus discovery requests timed out.", "regressionAwareness": "Resource context reports no Tier 1 or Tier 2 remediation history and `regression_detected: false`; this approach therefore does not repeat a known failed remediation.", "alternativeHypotheses": "Considered probe misconfiguration, image pull failure, OOM/resource exhaustion, node failure, and Service configuration. Probe failures are downstream of the application exit; image pull and scheduling succeeded; logs show exit code 1 rather than OOMKilled; application usage was low; all failing pods share the same bad ConfigMap while the prior template is healthy; Service port/selector are consistent. Node disk/CPU pressure remains a contributing operational risk but does not explain the identical invalid-directive log.", "confidenceCalibration": "0.97: reduced from 1.0 by 0.02 because the provenance of the bad ConfigMap change was not available and by 0.01 because Prometheus/Alertmanager queries timed out. Direct logs, ConfigMap diff, pod status, and healthy previous ReplicaSet provide strong confirmation."}, "remediationTarget": {"kind": "ConfigMap", "name": "gateway-config-bad", "namespace": "demo-ingress"}, "contributingFactors": ["Deployment revision 2 references ConfigMap `gateway-config-bad` instead of the healthy revision's `gateway-config`.", "Liveness and readiness probes target port 8080, but the application terminates before serving that port.", "The node has approximately 97% filesystem utilization and CPU pressure, but application resource usage and failure symmetry point to configuration as the direct cause."]}}, "total_prompt_tokens": 55474, "total_completion_tokens": 1882}}, {"event_id":"237fa9d4-3389-4ae2-a5ec-cab925988d88","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:37:41+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.enrichment.completed","event_action":"enriched","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"ai-rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7","event_data":{"event_id": "a166b9ef-ae80-4358-b171-fa310ea48da0", "event_type": "aiagent.enrichment.completed", "incident_id": "ai-rr-4309bc63be09-b3625ff7", "root_owner_kind": "ConfigMap", "root_owner_name": "gateway-config-bad", "failed_detections": [], "owner_chain_length": 1, "root_owner_namespace": "demo-ingress", "detected_labels_summary": {"stateful": false, "cdiManaged": false, "hpaEnabled": false, "helmManaged": false, "pdbProtected": false, "git