ew": ""}}, {"event_id":"cf1b2884-b65a-49d8-bd39-b8868ae25164","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:42:17+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.llm.request","event_action":"llm_request","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641","event_data":{"model": "gpt-5.6-luna", "phase": "workflow_discovery", "event_id": "d7fbaab0-82ba-46c2-aa11-9a11a04d7a79", "event_type": "aiagent.llm.request", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641", "prompt_length": 9194, "prompt_preview": "RCA findings: The three crashing api-gateway replicas use `gateway-config-bad`, whose `invalid_directive: true` causes `demo-http-server:1.0.0` to exit with code 1 during startup; the Deployment template must be corrected to mount `gateway-config`.\n\nSelect the appropriate remediation workflow.", "toolsets_enabled": ["list_available_actions", "list_workflows", "get_workflow", "todo_write", "submit_result_with_workflow", "submit_result_no_workflow"], "workflow_discovery_context": {"prompt_labels_present": false, "signal_labels_present": true, "enrichment_labels_present": false}}}, {"event_id":"d693d8d1-42ce-4cf5-bd88-40146594597c","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:42:17+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.rca.complete","event_action":"llm_response","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641","event_data":{"event_id": "40fb42ff-6529-4742-96d5-2a7dcc35b390", "event_type": "aiagent.rca.complete", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641", "response_data": {"analysis": "The three crashing api-gateway replicas use `gateway-config-bad`, whose `invalid_directive: true` causes `demo-http-server:1.0.0` to exit with code 1 during startup; the Deployment template must be corrected to mount `gateway-config`.", "warnings": [], "timestamp": "2026-10-02T04:42:17Z", "confidence": 0.98, "incidentId": "rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641", "isActionable": true, "needsHumanReview": false, "rootCauseAnalysis": {"summary": "The three crashing api-gateway replicas use `gateway-config-bad`, whose `invalid_directive: true` causes `demo-http-server:1.0.0` to exit with code 1 during startup; the Deployment template must be corrected to mount `gateway-config`.", "severity": "critical", "causalChain": ["Signal: Pods `api-gateway-67b95bfdbf-f9hwq`, `-l8ph9`, and `-wktck` entered CrashLoopBackOff under Deployment `api-gateway`.", "Why? The container terminates immediately with exit code 1; logs state `invalid directive found in /etc/demo-http-server/config.yaml — aborting`.", "Why? The failing ReplicaSet mounts ConfigMap `gateway-config-bad`, whose `config.yaml` contains unsupported `invalid_directive: true`.", "Why? Deployment revision 2 changed the pod template to reference `gateway-config-bad`, while the healthy revision references `gateway-config` and uses the same image, node, probes, and resources.", "Root cause: The `api-gateway` Deployment pod template references the invalid ConfigMap `gateway-config-bad`; update the Deployment to mount the validated `gateway-config` (or remove the invalid directive from the referenced configuration)."], "dueDiligence": {"targetAccuracy": "Confirmed the Deployment is the correct remediation target despite being the signal's parent. The bad reference is in the Deployment pod template (`volumes[].configMap.name: gateway-config-bad`), and changing that template to the known-good `gateway-config` fixes the configuration for all affected child pods. The ReplicaSet and Pods are generated children and should not be edited directly. This is not a propagated node condition: node memory pressure is low, and failures correlate exactly with the new ReplicaSet/configuration.", "proportionality": "The issue is isolated to the revision-2 pod template: 3 updated replicas fail while 4 revision-1 replicas remain healthy. The Deployment is the most specific remediable object because one template change corrects all affected replicas and allows the controller to replace the bad ReplicaSet pods; editing individual Pods or the ReplicaSet would be temporary and controller-reverted. Node disk/CPU concerns are contributing operational risks, not the cause of this crash loop.", "scopeCompleteness": "Checked the named Deployment, both ReplicaSets in its rollout, all seven listed application pods with up to three failing representatives, events for the named failing pod, both referenced ConfigMaps, pod logs and previous logs, pod resource usage, and node resource/condition statistics. The Service or external consumers were not inspected because the container fails before becoming ready and the signal is startup CrashLoopBackOff.", "causalCompleteness": "The chain reaches the deepest verified configuration cause: Deployment revision 2 -> `gateway-config-bad` -> unsupported directive -> process exit 1 -> CrashLoopBackOff. Application source or image internals were not available, but the runtime log explicitly identifies the invalid directive, so no deeper cause is needed for this incident.", "evidenceSufficiency": "Backed by Deployment and ReplicaSet specs, Pod status, current and previous logs, ConfigMap contents, events, resource usage, and node stats. Exact evidence includes exit code 1, log message `invalid directive`, the two ConfigMap names and contents, identical image digest, and healthy/failing replica comparison. Prometheus historical metrics and full node event history were not required to establish this cause and were not independently queried.", "regressionAwareness": "No prior remediation history is available for this target; enrichment reports empty Tier 1 and Tier 2 histories and `regression_detected: false`. The proposed change is a targeted correction of the ConfigMap reference, not a repeated failed remediation.", "alternativeHypotheses": "Considered OOMKilled/resource pressure, liveness-probe failure, image failure, node failure, and storage/disk pressure. OOM was contradicted by exit code 1, explicit application startup logs, low observed memory usage, and no memory pressure. Probe failure was contradicted because the process aborts during startup before serving; events show starts followed by back-off, not probe failures. Image failure is contradicted by the same image digest running healthy in four pods. Node failure is contradicted by healthy and failing pods sharing the node. Disk pressure is a risk on the node but does not explain the configuration-specific log or healthy peers.", "confidenceCalibration": "0.98. Starting from 1.0, reduced 0.01 because application source-level validation was unavailable and 0.01 because historical Prometheus/event data was not independently queried. Confidence remains high because the same explicit fatal log, exit code, bad ConfigMap content, and healthy control group directly isolate the cause."}, "remediationTarget": {"kind": "Deployment", "name": "api-gateway", "namespace": "demo-ingress"}, "contributingFactors": ["ReplicaSet `api-gateway-67b95bfdbf` revision 2 references ConfigMap `gateway-config-bad` instead of the working `gateway-config`.", "ConfigMap `gateway-config-bad` contains the unsupported `invalid_directive: true`; the healthy ConfigMap does not.", "The Deployment rollout created 3 failing updated replicas while 4 revision-1 replicas remained healthy, leaving `availableReplicas: 4` and `unavailableReplicas: 3."]}}, "total_prompt_tokens": 51204, "total_completion_tokens": 3207}}, {"event_id":"00b57dfc-10ea-408c-965f-343cdd72793b","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:42:17+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.llm.request","event_action":"same_kind_validation_gate","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641","event_data":{"model": "gpt-5.6-luna", "event_id": "76161e6f-f842-410f-b9a9-3977f0750df2", "event_type": "aiagent.llm.request", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641", "prompt_length": 43714, "retry_outcome": "resolved", "prompt_preview": "Your remediation_target.kind is \"Deployment\", which is the same resource kind as the input signal. Signals often propagate upward: workload-level issues 