rkflow.catalog.workflows_listed", "action_type": "RollbackDeployment", "search_metadata": {"duration_ms": 1}}}, {"event_id":"2e7870eb-4a61-42e5-a80e-fccc6d84ea2b","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:42:23+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.llm.tool_call","event_action":"tool_execution","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641","event_data":{"event_id": "61e71608-8226-409e-91ea-752836aeadbe", "tool_name": "list_workflows", "event_type": "aiagent.llm.tool_call", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641", "tool_result": {"workflows": [{"name": "fix-image-reference-v1", "version": "1.6.3", "workflowId": "45c70620-7fc4-5150-9165-ddc643b9281f", "description": {"what": "Corrects a Deployment's container image reference by reverting to the last known-good image from rollout history, recovering pods stuck in ImagePullBackOff due to a wrong tag or registry URL", "whenToUse": "When pods are stuck in ImagePullBackOff or ErrImagePull because the container image reference points to a non-existent tag, a wrong registry URL, or a deleted image. The Deployment has at least one previous revision with a valid image in its ReplicaSet history. Common after botched image promotions, typos in CI/CD pipelines, or premature tag deletions.", "whenNotToUse": "When the image pull failure is caused by expired or missing ImagePullSecrets (authentication issue) — use RefreshImagePullSecret instead. When the registry itself is down or rate-limiting — wait for recovery. When all revisions use the same broken image (no good revision to revert to).", "preconditions": "The Deployment has at least one previous ReplicaSet with a valid, pullable container image. The registry hosting the known-good image is accessible."}, "workflowName": "fix-image-reference-v1"}], "actionType": "RollbackDeployment"}, "tool_arguments": {"action_type": "RollbackDeployment"}, "tool_call_index": 0, "tool_result_preview": "{\"actionType\":\"RollbackDeployment\",\"workflows\":[{\"workflowId\":\"45c70620-7fc4-5150-9165-ddc643b9281f\",\"workflowName\":\"fix-image-reference-v1\",\"name\":\"fix-image-reference-v1\",\"description\":{\"what\":\"Corrects a Deployment's container image reference by reverting to the last known-good image from rollout history, recovering pods stuck in ImagePullBackOff due to a wrong tag or registry URL\",\"whenToUse\":\"When pods are stuck in ImagePullBackOff or ErrImagePull because the container image reference point"}}, {"event_id":"75a4850b-80c7-4ea2-97ee-148aa0262dca","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:42:26+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.response.complete","event_action":"response_sent","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641","event_data":{"event_id": "c70e004b-9422-4146-8471-fc4f7db4358a", "event_type": "aiagent.response.complete", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641", "response_data": {"analysis": "The Deployment pod template references gateway-config-bad, whose invalid_directive setting causes demo-http-server startup failure. The template should mount the known-good gateway-config ConfigMap.", "warnings": [], "timestamp": "2026-10-02T04:42:26Z", "confidence": 0.96, "incidentId": "rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641", "isActionable": true, "needsHumanReview": false, "selectedWorkflow": {"confidence": 0.96, "parameters": {"TARGET_RESOURCE_KIND": "Deployment", "TARGET_RESOURCE_NAME": "api-gateway", "TARGET_RESOURCE_NAMESPACE": "demo-ingress", "TARGET_RESOURCE_API_VERSION": "apps/v1"}, "workflowId": "45c70620-7fc4-5150-9165-ddc643b9281f", "executionBundle": "quay.io/kubernaut-cicd/test-workflows/fix-image-reference-job@sha256:0c3594fdf6d737b18a6aae6c63db677baa8673c7401ae3057ccbd7324819e0ae"}, "rootCauseAnalysis": {"summary": "The Deployment pod template references gateway-config-bad, whose invalid_directive setting causes demo-http-server startup failure. The template should mount the known-good gateway-config ConfigMap.", "severity": "critical", "causalChain": ["Signal: Pods `api-gateway-67b95bfdbf-f9hwq`, `-l8ph9`, and `-wktck` entered CrashLoopBackOff under Deployment `api-gateway`.", "Why? The container terminates immediately with exit code 1; logs state `invalid directive found in /etc/demo-http-server/config.yaml — aborting`.", "Why? The failing ReplicaSet mounts ConfigMap `gateway-config-bad`, whose `config.yaml` contains unsupported `invalid_directive: true`.", "Why? Deployment revision 2 changed the pod template to reference `gateway-config-bad`, while the healthy revision references `gateway-config` and uses the same image, node, probes, and resources.", "Root cause: The `api-gateway` Deployment pod template references the invalid ConfigMap `gateway-config-bad`; update the Deployment to mount the validated `gateway-config` (or remove the invalid directive from the referenced configuration)."], "dueDiligence": {"targetAccuracy": "Confirmed the Deployment is the correct remediation target despite being the signal's parent. The bad reference is in the Deployment pod template (`volumes[].configMap.name: gateway-config-bad`), and changing that template to the known-good `gateway-config` fixes the configuration for all affected child pods. The ReplicaSet and Pods are generated children and should not be edited directly. This is not a propagated node condition: node memory pressure is low, and failures correlate exactly with the new ReplicaSet/configuration.", "proportionality": "The issue is isolated to the revision-2 pod template: 3 updated replicas fail while 4 revision-1 replicas remain healthy. The Deployment is the most specific remediable object because one template change corrects all affected replicas and allows the controller to replace the bad ReplicaSet pods; editing individual Pods or the ReplicaSet would be temporary and controller-reverted. Node disk/CPU concerns are contributing operational risks, not the cause of this crash loop.", "scopeCompleteness": "Checked the named Deployment, both ReplicaSets in its rollout, all seven listed application pods with up to three failing representatives, events for the named failing pod, both referenced ConfigMaps, pod logs and previous logs, pod resource usage, and node resource/condition statistics. The Service or external consumers were not inspected because the container fails before becoming ready and the signal is startup CrashLoopBackOff.", "causalCompleteness": "The chain reaches the deepest verified configuration cause: Deployment revision 2 -> `gateway-config-bad` -> unsupported directive -> process exit 1 -> CrashLoopBackOff. Application source or image internals were not available, but the runtime log explicitly identifies the invalid directive, so no deeper cause is needed for this incident.", "evidenceSufficiency": "Backed by Deployment and ReplicaSet specs, Pod status, current and previous logs, ConfigMap contents, events, resource usage, and node stats. Exact evidence includes exit code 1, log message `invalid directive`, the two ConfigMap names and contents, identical image digest, and healthy/failing replica comparison. Prometheus historical metrics and full node event history were not required to establish this cause and were not independently queried.", "regressionAwareness": "No prior remediation history is available for this target; enrichment reports empty Tier 1 and Tier 2 histories and `regression_detected: false`. The proposed change is a targeted correction of the ConfigMap reference, not a repeated failed remediation.", "alternativeHypotheses": "Considered OOMKilled/resource pressure, liveness-probe failure, image failure, node failure, and storage/disk pressure. OOM was contradicted by exit code 1, explicit application startup logs, low observed memory usage, and no memory pressure. Probe failure was contradicted because the process aborts during startup before serving; events show starts followed by back-off, not probe failures. Image failure is contradicted by the same image digest running healthy in four pods. Node failure is contradicted by healthy and failing pods sharing the node. Disk pressure is a risk on the node but does not explain the configuration-specific log or healthy peers.", "confidenceCalibration": "0.98. Starting from 1.0, reduced 0.01 because application source-level validation was unavailable and 0.01 because historical Prometheus/event data was not independently queried. Confidence remains high because the same explicit fatal log, exit code, bad ConfigMap content, and healthy control group directly isolate the cause."}, "remediationTarget": {"kind": "Deployment", "name": "api-gateway", "namespace": "demo-ingress"}, "contributingFactors": ["Deployment revision 2 changed the ConfigMap reference from gateway-config to gateway-config-bad.", "gateway-config-bad contains unsupported invalid_directive: true, causing exit code 1.", "The previous revision using gateway-config remains healthy."]}, "alternativeWorkflows": [{"rationale": "Considered because the mounted ConfigMap contains an invalid directive, but its guidance says not to use it when the Deployment spec changed the ConfigMap name; the RCA confirms that template change.", "confidence": 0.55, "workflowId": "5abcef80-b22d-5c17-ae27-e9949cf8fb1e"}]}, "total_prompt_tokens": 85433, "total_completion_tokens": 3693}}, {"event_id":"dfcf9119-1eea-4598-ab36-0f6910004bdb","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:42:26+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.llm.request","event_action":"workflow_target_alignment_gate","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641","event_data":{"model": "", "event_id": "b0b0541d-8cb0-44ae-90a8-5174ff8b69e5", "event_type": "aiagent.llm.request", "incident_id": "rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641", "prompt_length": 0, "prompt_preview": ""}}, {"event_id":"d40c69ad-c6a4-41cc-ac7e-3a3a20f9623e","event_timestamp":"2026-10-02T04:42:26+00:00","event_type":"aiagent.session.completed","event_action":"session_completed","event_outcome":"success","correlation_id":"rr-4309bc63be09-59d3c641","event_data":{"event_id": "fca8251a-7067-42ed-92e7-